module ImportInnerAndTrailingMultiline exposing (v)

-- A multi-row comment INSIDE an import (between `import` and the module name)
-- and a multi-row comment TRAILING the same import, together.
--
-- `Formatter.Logical.Comments` merges the two into ONE sibling `OriginalRows`,
-- whose span then straddles the import: the comment node covers rows 24-26
-- while `import Foo2` is recorded at 25. `writtenInsideNodeAtIdx` asked whether
-- the comment ENDS on the import's first row, which is the same question only
-- while the comment stops there -- so neither of `sortImportGroups`' row rules
-- claimed it, the run broke at that point, and the first format left `Qux0`
-- above `Foo2` while the second sorted them. The predicate now asks
-- CONTAINMENT.
--
-- Four of the five spellings are stable: the inner comment alone, the trailing
-- one alone, and either of them written on a single row. Only both-multi-row
-- reaches it, which is why no hand-written fixture had it -- `gen-random.py`
-- v1.38 found it the first run it could emit the position at all.
--
-- This order happened to be the one that worked: it pins the sorter's row rule.
-- `ImportInnerCommentSortsEitherOrder` pins the same two imports written the
-- OTHER way round, which needed the unit's row EXTENT as well.


import Qux0
import {- k1
   bravo -} Foo2 {- k2
   tango -}


v =
    0
